ated but while  this doesn't happen  israel is changing things on the ground  and palestinians feel that what's going  on in shakhtar  is part of a much larger pattern of  annexation and dispossession  this has happened across palestine where  israel  allows itself to appropriate land  and houses on a really  false legal pretext so let's bring up  our map again  israeli forces were cracking down on  protesters in  sheikh jarrah for several days then on  may 7th  in the old city tens of thousands of men  women and children were at the final  friday prayers of ramadan  at the al-aqsa mosque one of the holiest  sites in islam  afterwards there were protests in the  old city but israeli forces raided the  mosque's compound  they threw stun grenades and fired  rubber-coated steel bullets at  palestinians  some of whom were throwing stones and it  spiraled from there  by the following monday there was tear  gas inside the mosque itself  the sea it laid siege to was incredibly  emotional for a lot of people around the  world  this is where gaza comes back in it's a  small strip of land where nearly 2  million palestinians are  crammed in they can't get out easily  because for the last 14 years  israel has imposed a land air and sea  blockade  and gaza is run by hamas a palestinian  group that israel and the u.s consider  terrorists now after all the violence in  east jerusalem  the top commander of hamas warned israel  that it had until 6 pm that monday  to withdraw its security forces from the  al-aqsa mosque compound  and jerusalem's sheikshana neighborhood  when the deadline passed  hamas fired rockets into central israel  and israel's military attacked  they destroyed this building after  warning people inside to leave  then hamas responded again this is a  wave after wave  of attacks coming out of gaza now these  rockets  are heading in the direction of tel aviv  from there it just got worse  relentless air attacks by the israelis  and thousands of rockets launched by