ans their basic  rights  it's a system that human rights watch  and others have described as apartheid  they are not equal or full citizens  indeed they're incredibly marginalized  and discriminated against the us as  israel's most important ally  has a special role to play in this  people are looking to president joe  biden to see whether he'll say or do  things differently from previous  administrations  he hasn't so far my expectation and hope  is that  this will be uh closing down sooner than  later  but israel has a right to defend itself  when you have thousands of rockets  flying into  your territory but we've been here  before  and to avoid being here again something  has to change  the only way that this will end is with  full decolonization  palestinian liberation the divide is not  necessarily right now between  jews and arabs between those who believe  that can be  a coexistence reconciliation that the  two people can live in peace in the same  and  respecting each other and those who  don't think like this  right now that idea of peaceful  coexistence  may seem impossibly far off but the  answer  can't be to just keep going like this  [Music]  hopefully that was a useful starting  point but obviously there is so much  more context to this story on  aljazeera.com we've got data  interactives  plenty of analysis and a live blog with  all the latest  i'll see you next week  you

